l fail but in practice it was always easy to find a value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" where the center of gravity is quite far from the actual center. Another way to probabilistically test if the center of gravity is at the center is to choose a random prime "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1, and a random "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/310166033646ce6deba8aa3544a95cfcd6a66d99f72f67c6a099dba1e1ed5faf.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then it must be the case that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/1b62637ce52f9d68d6b36c33bc36fa08614b3afe0e0701848813ec122c5a6009.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/54572"}